...A woman holds me.
The woman is Mother.

Another person, a man, faces Mother.
—Father.

Mother speaks to Father one word at a time, driving each into him.

&quot;You are not her father.&quot;

Mother speaks.

&quot;You must not think yourself this child&#x27;s father.&quot;

&quot;This child is my daughter alone.&quot;

&quot;This child has no father.&quot;

&quot;This child is not your daughter.&quot;

Father listens in silence.

His expression tells me he possesses no freedom to choose.
Mother merely informs him of a decision already made.

She repeats herself.

&quot;This child has no father.&quot;

—I have no father.

&quot;You are not this child&#x27;s father.&quot;

—This person is not my father.

&quot;You must not...<span class="beat" aria-label="Pause">◆</span>love this child.&quot;

I shall not—
Be loved by this person.
